Ticket #4471 contains reports merged by intake. This view deduplicates repeated export rows by report ID. The intake tag is a guess; the cause follows each tenant's locale and booking form.

## Causes in the export

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser: day and month flipped

The shared parser reads dates month-first even when a tenant's locale writes day-first. This cause covers app, email, and booking-v2 form reports across the day-first tenants.

**GitHub follow-up:** [Issue #1](https://github.com/MichalMatak/knowledge-base/issues/1).

## Booking-v3 hint conflicts with a day-first locale

The booking-v3 form shows an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint for day-first tenants. Customers following that hint enter a month-first date, while the form parses it according to the tenant's day-first locale. This cause covers Alder Physio (`de-DE`), Copper Studio (`es-ES`), and Pale Harbour (`pt-PT`).

**GitHub follow-up:** [Issue #2](https://github.com/MichalMatak/knowledge-base/issues/2).

## One-day moves

The desk notes flag `R-41202`, `R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, and `R-41620` as one-day moves. The tenant/form rule still places them in the shared-parser group; the notes do not establish a third cause.

